  "limits": [
    "This corrects internal native resource ownership; no new GUI action or visible app layout is added. No synthetic screenshot is used as acceptance. The separate published preset-startup/Save screenshots are not counted as copy validation.",
    "Resource JSON and live icon are distinct representations: direct pixel writes still do not automatically update serialized PNG, dirty state or preview caches. Explicit set_icon reserializes pixels. Copy takes the live pixels, not a re-decoding of potentially stale PNG.",
    "set_icon retains its input object and ref_icon returns an owning mutable reference. This patch changes generic copy independence only, not these APIs.",
    "Allocation failure is source-reviewed only, not deterministically fault-injected. A failed pixbuf allocation throws inside the existing C++ exception boundary before target replacement/dirtying. The native void copy API cannot return an error; native duplication can still return a constructed default object after a contained copy failure.",
    "Native generic duplicate deliberately clears name/file; native copy preserves destination name and self-copy is a no-op. Legacy name-preserving export and named-handle disposition remain open.",
    "AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer run the same seven registrations with fatal diagnostics and unchanged 60/120-second bounds. LeakSanitizer is disabled.",
    "Existing build/test fixture plug-in notices remain disclosed; exact libcloudproviders DEBUG bus-absence notices are narrowly checked and machine IDs normalized in this report. No unexpected warning, critical, sanitizer diagnostic, skipped case or failed process is accepted.",
